46	AMD	yearly	1970	AMD's first full year of operations saw the company establish itself as a reliable manufacturer of bipolar logic integrated circuits. In March 1970, AMD shipped its first products including the Am9300 4-bit MSI shift register and Am2505 high-speed shift register. The company also produced its first proprietary product, the Am2501 logic counter chip, which became highly successful in the market. By year-end 1970, AMD employed 53 people and had developed 18 different products, though the company had not yet generated significant revenue. The focus was on establishing manufacturing quality and reliability, positioning AMD as a viable second-source alternative to established semiconductor manufacturers. AMD's strategy during this period centered on providing products that could serve as compatible alternatives to industry-standard components, a business model that would define much of the company's early growth.	AMD's first year of operations ended with 53 employees and 18 products developed, though no revenue was recorded yet. The company shipped its first products in March 1970, including the Am9300 shift register and the proprietary Am2501 logic counter.	["Wikipedia - Advanced Micro Devices", "History of Advanced Micro Devices - FundingUniverse", "The Story of Advanced Micro Devices - Medium"]	2026-03-26 22:49:07
